  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "87d19fba-b482-4e02-8a27-a5997078bc23",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Interpretation of the Result"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4af79714-6640-4ffd-8808-fe80726e45c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- The dataset was successfully reshaped from long to wide format, enabling easier comparison of hospital admission measures across organisations.\n",
    "- Missing values after pivoting indicate measures that were not reported or not applicable to specific organisations.\n",
    "- No negative admission values were observed, suggesting logical consistency in reported measures.\n",
    "- The automated checks demonstrated how data quality can be assessed systematically before downstream analysis.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7ee25701-20cd-4576-b741-8dc4e41a5552",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why This Project Is Relevant"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7250199-d4d4-4214-b03b-4939f6ffc169",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This project addresses real challenges faced in healthcare analytics, where data is frequently released in complex, long formats and must be validated before use.\n",
    "\n",
    "The same approach demonstrated here can be applied to:\n",
    "- Insurance claims processing\n",
    "- Hospital operations dashboards\n",
    "- Public health surveillance systems\n",
    "- Sales and operational data in non-healthcare industries\n",
    "\n",
    "By automating data quality checks, organisations reduce the risk of making decisions based on incomplete or inconsistent data.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "6a2f947f-a688-4b0b-baf1-ec4b2bd7a080",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_data_quality_pipeline(csv_path):\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        df = pd.read_csv(csv_path)\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        return {\"status\": \"FAILED\", \"error\": str(e)}\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Schema validation\n",
    "    expected_columns = [\"UID\", \"Code\", \"Category\", \"Measure\", \"Measure_Value\"]\n",
    "    missing_cols = [col for col in expected_columns if col not in df.columns]\n",
    "    if missing_cols:\n",
    "        return {\n",
    "            \"status\": \"FAILED\",\n",
    "            \"missing_columns\": missing_cols\n",
    "        }\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Data quality checks\n",
    "    missing_values = df.isna().sum().to_dict()\n",
    "    duplicate_rows = int(df.duplicated().sum())\n",
    "    negative_values = int((df[\"Measure_Value\"] < 0).sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "    dtype_issues = {\n",
    "        col: str(dtype)\n",
    "        for col, dtype in df.dtypes.items()\n",
    "        if col == \"Measure_Value\" and not pd.api.types.is_numeric_dtype(dtype)\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    quality_report = {\n",
    "        \"missing_values\": missing_values,\n",
    "        \"duplicate_rows\": duplicate_rows,\n",
    "        \"negative_values\": negative_values,\n",
    "        \"dtype_warnings\": dtype_issues\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Fail pipeline on critical violations\n",
    "    if negative_values > 0:\n",
    "        return {\n",
    "            \"status\": \"FAILED\",\n",
    "            \"quality_report\": quality_report\n",
    "        }\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Transformation\n",
    "    wide_df = df.pivot_table(\n",
    "        index=[\"UID\", \"Code\", \"Category\"],\n",
    "        columns=\"Measure\",\n",
    "        values=\"Measure_Value\",\n",
    "        aggfunc=\"sum\"\n",
    "    ).reset_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"status\": \"SUCCESS\",\n",
    "        \"quality_report\": quality_report,\n",
    "        \"processed_data\": wide_df\n",
    "    }\n"
   ]
  },
